Good idea.  I think the capital Y/N is the best solution.


On a related topic, something else I'd like to see would be customizable
"translations" in the X11 interface.  I realize translations are a feature
of Xt, but... well, it seems like most programs that get this big
tend to have facilities for re-binding keys. (The keypad option
is a good start.)

Another possibility would be to put a layer of customization between
ascii characters and commands.  It would be as platform-independant as
it is now, and you could have ctrl- and meta-characters.

But it would be nice to take advantage of function keys through X11.
With 12 function keys, I could just about eliminate use of the Ctrl
and Shift keys, thus cutting down on RSI discomfort.

